👉 Replit = where you can develop and test your code.
👉 Lambda = where AWS can execute that code serverlessly.

=========

| Replit                              | AWS Lambda                           |
| ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------------ |
| Online development environment      | Serverless execution service         |
| Used to write/test code             | Used to run deployed code            |
| You develop your Python application | AWS executes your function           |
| Like an online coding workspace     | Like an AWS-managed function runtime |


=========

Replit is an online coding and development platform.

Think of it as a cloud-based coding workspace where you can write and run Python code without installing Python or setting up a development environment on your computer.

Simple example

Normally:

Your Computer
   ↓
Install Python
   ↓
Write Python Code
   ↓
Run Code

With Replit:

Browser
   ↓
Replit
   ↓
Write Python Code
   ↓
Run Code
In your AWS workflow

If your course says:

“Replit code → AWS Lambda Functions”

it means:

Replit
   ↓
Develop & test your Python application
   ↓
Take the working code
   ↓
AWS Lambda
   ↓
Deploy it as a serverless function

